        <mxCell id="e8bXX2RFwwMwmefmS9Mo-69" value="Order your fringe by priority values. You should use the same alphabetical&lt;br/&gt;tie-breaking scheme when choosing the order of the fringe. Make sure you include&lt;br/&gt;the {} symbols in your answer&amp;nbsp;&lt;div&gt;(a) Give the state of the priority queue after S is visited in the format shown&lt;br/&gt;above.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;(b) Give the state of the priority queue after B is visited.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;(c) Give the state of the priority queue after Prim’s is complete.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;(d) For the graph above, what is the order in which edges are added to the MST&lt;br/&gt;when running Kruskal’s Algorithm. Your answer should be in the form of a&lt;br/&gt;comma separated list with spaces.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;S, A, E, B, F, I, C, G, D, H&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=15;" vertex="1" parent="1">
